WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do want to have this --
Well, I've been asking people,

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you think Trump
is a worse client,

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
or Rudy Giuliani is
a worse lawyer?"

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where do you come out on that?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, this is
a very difficult question.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is, right?
-Uh, I would say --

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is like a question
that, like, in order

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get over a bridge,
like, a troll would ask you.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Monty Python
and the Holy Grail."

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-I -- I would say

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Rudy Giuliani is perhap
the worst lawyer

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
that anyone could have.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I would point to this
which just came out

00:00:29.396 --> 00:00:30.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
within the last 24 hours.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
In "The New Yorker,"
Giuliani quoted as saying,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had to get rid of
Yovanovitch,

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:39.773 size:81% position:41%
this courageous former
ambassador to Ukraine,

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she was going to
get in the way

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:42.275 size:88% position:44% line:92%
of these investigations.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:47.614
I mean, it was just anothe
full-throated confession.

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And so I don't know

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
what kind of malpractice
that is,

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:56.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
but nonetheless, you know,
on a serious note,

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.324 size:84% position:42% line:92%
what he has admitted --

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
what the president
has admitted --

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the president is
out on the White House lawn,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's asked, "What did yo
want on that phone call,

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the president,
in his own words,

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:07.634 size:88% position:44% line:92%
asked for this favor --"

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.836
the Ukraine president brings up,
"We need more military help,

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the president said,
"But I have a favor, though" -

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.474 line:92%
"what did you want him to do?"

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:15.675 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And the president says,

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, if we're being honest
about it,

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.511 size:78% position:39% line:92%
it's a simple answer.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
He should investigate
the Bidens."

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.247 size:81% position:41%
And it was interesting
because he was asked

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
about, "What did you want
at the time?"

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
but his answer was
what he wants right now.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
He still wants an investigatio
of the Bidens.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if not by Ukraine,
then by China.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this was why
we felt an imperative

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
to move forward with
the articles of impeachmen

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:34.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that we did,

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the threat
is ongoing.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.398 line:92%
The plot has never stopped

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
His efforts to get
foreign countries

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
to help him cheat
in the next election

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:45.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
are a continuing threat
to our democracy.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:49.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he continues,
and his lawyer continues,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make the case
for his own removal.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.912 size:78% position:39%
-And yet, obviously,
we're in a situation,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on what would have t
happen in the Senate,

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is very unlikely
that he is going to be voted

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be impeached
and out of office.

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
You mentioned, like,
this is something

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're going to say
to your grandkids

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:05.058
what you did in this moment.
Do you feel as though, you know,

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
if the outcome is
what can be expected,

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:08.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is he's not going to
leave office from this,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:12.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
has it been worth it
to impeach him in the House,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
which obviously will happe
on Wednesday?

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.171 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.540 size:81% position:41%
Again, if they were --
If they were senators,

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:23.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'd be in a whole different
situation right now.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The answer is yes.
And I say that --

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was someone
who was reluctant

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.315 size:78% position:39% line:92%
to go down this road.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
But two things
changed my mind.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first was
this latest misconduct

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
involving this shakedown
of a country at war.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:40.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a shakedown that damages
our own national security

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.461 line:92%
was just a bridge too far.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
But also it was
the issue of timing.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:46.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
The day after
Bob Mueller testified,

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.801 line:92%
the day after he talked abou

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.937 size:78% position:39%
Russia's interference
in our last election,

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
how they might interfere
in the next election,

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump believes
it's finally over.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:59.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the next day, he's on th
phone with Zelensky,

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.748 line:92%
asking for yet another country

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:03.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
to intervene
in yet another election.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:06.352
That said to me, this presiden
believes he is above the law

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
accountable to no one,
can't be indicted,

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's got his Roy Cohn
in Bill Barr

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the Justice Department,
can't be impeached,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
he is utterly beyond
any form of accountability

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:21.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is too dangerous a
situation to go unchallenged

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.969 line:92%
And so we do what we must.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.070 line:92%
The fact that the Republican

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
may or may not honor
their Constitutional duty

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.508 size:75% position:38%
doesn't mean that we
relinquish our own.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right, thanks so much
for being here.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's Adam Schiff.

